WEBVTT

00:01:37.720 --> 00:01:38.850
Morning.

00:01:40.470 --> 00:01:41.480
Morning.

00:01:45.700 --> 00:01:47.540
Why so spacey today?

00:01:47.540 --> 00:01:49.170
Sleep with your belly uncovered?

00:01:49.610 --> 00:01:51.120
No, I didn't!

00:01:51.490 --> 00:01:52.490
How many?

00:01:52.490 --> 00:01:53.630
Three!

00:01:56.480 --> 00:01:57.920
Where's Dad?

00:01:58.380 --> 00:01:59.690
Morning meeting.

00:02:00.220 --> 00:02:02.290
He's been really busy, lately.

00:02:03.000 --> 00:02:05.350
I hope he's taking care of himself.

00:02:05.350 --> 00:02:07.680
If that's how you feel, don't make him worry.

00:02:09.020 --> 00:02:11.270
I heard you came home soaking wet.

00:02:11.270 --> 00:02:13.550
Oh! Just a little.

00:02:14.100 --> 00:02:16.820
And I had a bath as soon as I got home.

00:02:19.150 --> 00:02:21.120
But then you slept, belly uncovered.

00:02:21.120 --> 00:02:22.570
I did not!

00:02:25.730 --> 00:02:27.210
Thanks for the pancakes.

00:02:34.050 --> 00:02:35.390
Wh-What?

00:02:36.000 --> 00:02:37.720
Still going on, huh?

00:02:37.720 --> 00:02:39.030
What is?

00:02:42.740 --> 00:02:44.690
Eat that and grow up big.

00:02:45.280 --> 00:02:48.950
You used to say you'd grow as 
tall as an electric pole, right?

00:02:49.390 --> 00:02:51.180
Here. Take these, too.

00:02:51.180 --> 00:02:53.700
This is just because you hate broccoli!

00:02:53.700 --> 00:02:59.700
<b>Sakura and the Lovely Transfer Student</b>

00:03:02.330 --> 00:03:05.080
Your brother is so funny, Sakura-chan!

00:03:05.080 --> 00:03:07.300
No, he's just mean.

00:03:07.300 --> 00:03:09.070
How were the pancakes?

00:03:09.530 --> 00:03:12.560
Well... They were good, of course.

00:03:12.560 --> 00:03:13.830
Good morning.

00:03:14.690 --> 00:03:16.700
Take your seats, everyone!

00:03:16.700 --> 00:03:18.090
Yes, ma'am!

00:03:19.560 --> 00:03:23.210
Today, I have a new classmate 
to introduce to you.

00:03:25.690 --> 00:03:27.060
Shinomoto-san!

00:03:39.600 --> 00:03:41.040
Introduce yourself.

00:03:41.560 --> 00:03:42.480
Okay.

00:03:44.650 --> 00:03:46.250
I'm Akiho Shinomoto.

00:03:47.070 --> 00:03:48.770
I look forward to joining your class.

00:03:56.020 --> 00:03:57.940
Her name is written like this.

00:03:58.340 --> 00:04:01.790
You'll all have to teach her lots about 
Tomoeda Middle School, okay?

00:04:01.800 --> 00:04:03.800
<b>Akiho Shinomoto</b>

00:04:02.160 --> 00:04:03.800
So, you'll be added to the rotation

00:04:03.800 --> 00:04:06.810
for day duty and classroom tasks, next week.

00:04:05.400 --> 00:04:07.120
She's very pretty, isn't she?

00:04:06.810 --> 00:04:09.570
I'll update the class roster, 
so be sure to check it.

00:04:07.120 --> 00:04:08.690
Yeah, really pretty!

00:04:10.310 --> 00:04:15.240
Tomorrow is the deadline to submit 
requests for extracurricular lessons.

00:04:10.780 --> 00:04:13.420
<i>I hope we can be friends.</i>

00:04:16.690 --> 00:04:17.650
Here, we go.

00:04:20.560 --> 00:04:22.790
Sorry we're late!

00:04:22.790 --> 00:04:24.130
No problem.

00:04:24.130 --> 00:04:24.710
Huh?

00:04:27.820 --> 00:04:29.200
Good afternoon.

00:04:29.200 --> 00:04:32.950
Hi. You must be the Class 2 transfer 
student everyone's talking about.

00:04:32.950 --> 00:04:34.630
Everyone's talking about her?

00:04:34.630 --> 00:04:37.890
One of the kids from our 
class went to take a look.

00:04:37.890 --> 00:04:38.960
Really?

00:04:39.400 --> 00:04:42.170
I invited her to eat lunch with us.

00:04:42.680 --> 00:04:44.090
Make yourself at home.

00:04:49.690 --> 00:04:51.810
What? You were in Hong Kong?

00:04:51.810 --> 00:04:54.310
Yes, before I came to Japan.

00:04:54.670 --> 00:04:59.540
She was in France before that, 
and Germany before that, and...

00:04:59.540 --> 00:05:02.130
She lived in Italy and England, as well.

00:05:02.130 --> 00:05:02.810
Yes.

00:05:02.810 --> 00:05:04.480
That's amazing!

00:05:04.480 --> 00:05:07.810
So I don't know if my Japanese is correct.

00:05:07.810 --> 00:05:08.910
It's fine!

00:05:08.910 --> 00:05:11.210
But there's no need to be so formal.

00:05:11.210 --> 00:05:12.820
We're all the same age.

00:05:13.670 --> 00:05:15.910
But this is how I learned it.

00:05:16.260 --> 00:05:17.660
Speaking of formalities...

00:05:17.660 --> 00:05:20.650
They're generally used when speaking 
to superiors and elders, right?

00:05:17.670 --> 00:05:35.810
<b>chatter                           chatter             chatter</b>

00:05:20.650 --> 00:05:22.520
But in one area of Japan,

00:05:22.520 --> 00:05:25.730
older people use formal language 
with younger people.

00:05:25.730 --> 00:05:28.130
They're very strict about 
manners and politeness.

00:05:28.130 --> 00:05:32.780
If you speak informally, even by accident, 
they'll get really mad!

00:05:32.780 --> 00:05:35.820
Scary, right? Scary, right? Too scary, right?

00:05:35.820 --> 00:05:39.150
Your lies have seemed kinda lazy, lately.

00:05:40.130 --> 00:05:41.060
I'll be careful!

00:05:42.330 --> 00:05:43.560
I'll be careful!

00:05:44.440 --> 00:05:47.810
You've created even more victims!

00:05:53.080 --> 00:05:56.640
Oh, I need to go see the teacher!

00:05:56.640 --> 00:05:58.350
In the faculty office?

00:05:58.350 --> 00:05:59.080
Yes.

00:05:59.080 --> 00:06:00.590
Do you know where it is?

00:06:01.930 --> 00:06:03.350
I'll show you!

00:06:03.350 --> 00:06:07.130
But the lunch break isn't over yet...

00:06:07.130 --> 00:06:09.480
We'll watch your things.

00:06:09.480 --> 00:06:10.490
But...

00:06:10.490 --> 00:06:11.910
Go ahead.

00:06:11.910 --> 00:06:13.330
U-Um...

00:06:14.920 --> 00:06:16.260
Let me show you the way.

00:06:20.060 --> 00:06:21.620
Thank you very much.

00:06:25.780 --> 00:06:29.220
Those two kind of make you 
feel all warm inside, huh?

00:06:29.220 --> 00:06:34.030
I haven't talked to Akiho-chan 
much, but she's really nice!

00:06:34.030 --> 00:06:35.020
She is.

00:06:35.020 --> 00:06:36.530
And she's so trusting!

00:06:36.900 --> 00:06:40.470
And you lied to a girl like her! Ugh!

00:06:42.360 --> 00:06:45.920
Even the way you're laughing feels lazy!

00:06:46.630 --> 00:06:49.130
I had to make your friends 
watch my lunch box...

00:06:49.130 --> 00:06:50.610
It's okay!

00:06:50.610 --> 00:06:54.730
Tomoyo-chan and Chiharu-chan will 
bring it back to the classroom.

00:06:56.880 --> 00:06:58.750
They're all very kind.

00:06:58.750 --> 00:07:01.730
Yeah, they really are.

00:07:02.560 --> 00:07:03.830
So are you.

00:07:04.980 --> 00:07:05.850
Me?

00:07:08.990 --> 00:07:10.350
You are kind!

00:07:12.030 --> 00:07:14.240
<b>Blush . . .</b>

00:07:14.480 --> 00:07:18.010
Come to think of it, we're a 
bit alike, aren't we?

00:07:19.270 --> 00:07:20.990
Sakura Kinomoto.

00:07:21.500 --> 00:07:23.790
Akiho Shinomoto-chan.

00:07:24.500 --> 00:07:27.990
They sort of sound alike, 
especially the last names.

00:07:28.310 --> 00:07:29.750
You're right.

00:07:31.300 --> 00:07:34.560
I would like for us to become 
friends, Sakura-san!

00:07:37.070 --> 00:07:38.380
Me, too!

00:07:40.520 --> 00:07:43.310
I'm so glad to know you, Sakura-san!

00:07:43.920 --> 00:07:45.880
Same to you!

00:07:51.760 --> 00:07:54.480
Okay, time to start afternoon classes!

00:07:58.930 --> 00:08:01.150
Japanese class makes me nervous...

00:08:01.150 --> 00:08:04.310
If there's anything you don't 
understand, feel free to ask us.

00:08:04.310 --> 00:08:06.000
Though, we might not be much help.

00:08:08.370 --> 00:08:10.260
I appreciate it very much.

00:08:10.570 --> 00:08:14.650
Today, we'll continue our lesson on 
four-character idiomatic compounds.

00:08:15.140 --> 00:08:17.220
Fill in the missing characters!

00:08:17.780 --> 00:08:19.180
Let's see... Ono-san.

00:08:19.180 --> 00:08:19.940
Yes, ma'am.

00:08:19.940 --> 00:08:20.900
Toomi-san.

00:08:20.900 --> 00:08:21.610
Yes, ma'am.

00:08:21.610 --> 00:08:22.630
Wada-san.

00:08:22.630 --> 00:08:23.570
Y-Yes, ma'am!

00:08:23.570 --> 00:08:24.640
Kinomoto-san.

00:08:24.990 --> 00:08:25.590
Yes, ma'am!

00:08:25.590 --> 00:08:26.900
Come on up.

00:08:27.800 --> 00:08:29.240
Good luck.

00:08:29.240 --> 00:08:30.660
I'm rooting for you.

00:08:30.660 --> 00:08:32.110
I-I'll try.

00:08:40.560 --> 00:08:41.790
You can do it!

00:08:48.290 --> 00:08:48.880
<b>Plain as day        Touch-and-go        Anything and        The strongest</b>

00:08:48.290 --> 00:08:48.880
<b>everything              one there is</b>

00:08:48.880 --> 00:08:54.050
<b>Plain as day        Touch-and-go        Anything and</b>

00:08:48.880 --> 00:08:54.050
<b>everything</b>

00:08:51.630 --> 00:08:53.390
You're all correct!

00:08:53.390 --> 00:08:54.040
Yes!

00:09:09.750 --> 00:09:11.310
S-Sorry...

00:09:13.080 --> 00:09:14.920
Okay, here's the next set of problems.

00:09:15.490 --> 00:09:17.840
What's the matter, Sakura-chan?

00:09:18.880 --> 00:09:20.400
Oh, uh...

00:09:20.400 --> 00:09:24.160
Sakura-san, you got it on the 
first try! That was amazing!

00:09:24.160 --> 00:09:26.660
No, I just remembered studying that one.

00:09:27.200 --> 00:09:29.570
<i>I just imagined that, right?</i>

00:09:36.300 --> 00:09:38.080
S-S-Sorry!

00:09:47.240 --> 00:09:48.890
What in the world is wrong, Kinomoto-san?

00:09:49.660 --> 00:09:51.730
U-Um, I...

00:09:55.250 --> 00:09:57.530
I saw something weird outside again!

00:09:59.910 --> 00:10:03.930
Sensei, Kinomoto-san says 
she isn't feeling well.

00:10:07.970 --> 00:10:09.630
A-Are you all right?

00:10:09.630 --> 00:10:12.090
Um, y-yes! No! I mean...

00:10:12.090 --> 00:10:14.000
May I take her to the nurse's office?

00:10:14.280 --> 00:10:17.010
You're on the health committee, aren't you?

00:10:15.090 --> 00:10:16.440
Sakura-chan...

00:10:17.320 --> 00:10:18.770
Will you two be all right?

00:10:18.770 --> 00:10:19.500
Yes.

00:10:19.850 --> 00:10:20.920
Let's go.

00:10:26.270 --> 00:10:28.550
<i>Sorry, Akiho-chan!</i>

00:10:33.140 --> 00:10:35.350
Nobody else is around.

00:10:35.830 --> 00:10:39.520
I'm sorry to drag you out of class for this!

00:10:39.520 --> 00:10:43.440
Don't worry about me. 
It seemed like an emergency.

00:10:43.920 --> 00:10:46.710
But what happened, so suddenly?

00:10:47.960 --> 00:10:49.950
The trees in the courtyard were moving!

00:10:49.950 --> 00:10:53.520
At first, it was just one... just one 
tree that started walking.

00:10:53.520 --> 00:10:55.650
But then more and more of them did it!

00:10:55.650 --> 00:10:57.950
Then, it's probably another...

00:10:58.450 --> 00:11:02.240
Yeah. It might be another new card.

00:11:05.880 --> 00:11:09.550
At last, the time has come to say that line.

00:11:21.970 --> 00:11:25.780
I thought this might happen, 
so I brought this costume...

00:11:26.120 --> 00:11:27.500
I thought this might happen,

00:11:27.800 --> 00:11:31.000
so I brought my camcorder, 
and they both proved useful!

00:11:31.720 --> 00:11:34.540
I wondered why you brought your bag.

00:11:34.540 --> 00:11:36.500
So this is why.

00:11:36.500 --> 00:11:40.480
Sakura-chan, do a little twirl!

00:11:41.370 --> 00:11:43.320
L-Like this?

00:11:46.260 --> 00:11:48.190
That's perfect!

00:11:48.180 --> 00:11:53.190
<b>zip                                  zip                     zip</b>

00:11:48.190 --> 00:11:50.160
Do some other poses.

00:11:50.160 --> 00:11:53.270
Oh, and hold the hem of your skirt!

00:12:04.410 --> 00:12:05.530
Sakura-chan!

00:12:11.740 --> 00:12:13.790
They're trying to leave the school grounds!

00:12:27.300 --> 00:12:29.610
<i>Key that hides the forces of dreams!</i>

00:12:31.280 --> 00:12:34.560
<i>Show me your true form!</i>

00:12:35.060 --> 00:12:37.030
<i>Release!</i>

00:12:55.830 --> 00:12:57.640
Stay here, Tomoyo-chan!

00:12:58.240 --> 00:12:59.330
Sakura-chan!

00:13:03.010 --> 00:13:04.210
Aqua?

00:13:04.620 --> 00:13:06.070
But watering the trees

00:13:06.070 --> 00:13:09.020
might just energize them and 
make them run faster.

00:13:09.750 --> 00:13:10.600
In that case...

00:13:11.070 --> 00:13:11.880
<i>Siege!</i>

00:13:26.180 --> 00:13:27.910
Now, they can't get out—

00:13:35.050 --> 00:13:36.620
W-Wait!

00:13:43.830 --> 00:13:45.410
What should I do?

00:13:46.730 --> 00:13:49.150
Make yourself more flexible!

00:14:06.050 --> 00:14:07.800
It's going to break!

00:14:10.690 --> 00:14:11.710
Maybe...

00:14:12.650 --> 00:14:14.110
If I use that card...

00:14:17.440 --> 00:14:19.220
But if I'm wrong...

00:14:28.960 --> 00:14:33.460
Water, fill the earth and 
halt their movement.

00:14:34.800 --> 00:14:35.800
<i>Aqua!</i>

00:15:03.010 --> 00:15:03.960
It worked.

00:15:08.920 --> 00:15:10.140
Now!

00:15:10.640 --> 00:15:12.670
Open a path before me!

00:15:25.410 --> 00:15:26.650
<i>Force without master,</i>

00:15:26.920 --> 00:15:30.570
<i>heed the call of my Staff of Dreams, 
and become my power!</i>

00:15:31.150 --> 00:15:32.110
<i>Secure!</i>

00:15:54.850 --> 00:15:56.640
<b>Action</b>

00:16:00.350 --> 00:16:01.660
Sakura-chan!

00:16:02.120 --> 00:16:03.340
Tomoyo-chan!

00:16:03.640 --> 00:16:05.570
We were right. It was a card.

00:16:08.410 --> 00:16:11.430
I finally got... to say my line...

00:16:11.890 --> 00:16:14.690
I even had the costume and camcorder ready!

00:16:15.610 --> 00:16:16.740
<i>Now!</i>

00:16:16.740 --> 00:16:18.130
<i>Open a path before me!</i>

00:16:18.130 --> 00:16:23.800
But I didn't arrange a way to film you 
while you're enclosed within magic!

00:16:27.230 --> 00:16:29.650
It was really hard on me...

00:16:29.650 --> 00:16:33.020
Both capturing the card and 
moving the trees back.

00:16:33.020 --> 00:16:35.310
I was afraid someone would see me.

00:16:35.310 --> 00:16:37.360
They didn't go back on their own?

00:16:37.360 --> 00:16:39.180
No, they didn't!

00:16:39.570 --> 00:16:43.030
I had to use this card again 
to make them move.

00:16:43.790 --> 00:16:47.090
I mean, Tomoyo-chan was glad 
she got to film me using magic

00:16:44.440 --> 00:16:50.280
<b>If you walk too fast, people will 
hear your roots hitting 
the ground, so move slowly!</b>

00:16:47.090 --> 00:16:50.140
She missed the first time because 
it was hidden by Siege, but...

00:16:50.140 --> 00:16:51.450
Rats!

00:16:51.450 --> 00:16:55.410
If I'd gone to school with you, my heroic 
deeds would've also been caught on video!

00:16:56.200 --> 00:16:59.690
So, what can this card do, anyway?

00:16:56.670 --> 00:17:00.010
I wanted to be filmed, too!

00:17:00.970 --> 00:17:02.370
Well...

00:17:03.400 --> 00:17:04.530
<i>Action.</i>

00:17:09.550 --> 00:17:11.480
It seems to make things move.

00:17:11.480 --> 00:17:14.320
But when the heck would you use that?

00:17:15.460 --> 00:17:17.090
It would make carrying tea easier.

00:17:17.090 --> 00:17:19.250
You're thinkin' on a pretty small scale!

00:17:19.250 --> 00:17:22.600
It can move trees, too! That's not small!

00:17:26.850 --> 00:17:28.950
I sense no magic in this, either.

00:17:30.070 --> 00:17:30.690
But...

00:17:31.600 --> 00:17:35.110
When you use that key, you can use its power.

00:17:35.980 --> 00:17:39.790
Perhaps the key lies in that staff.

00:17:41.580 --> 00:17:44.720
In other words, the staff is the key, so...

00:17:45.110 --> 00:17:48.380
Couldn't you also say, 
"The key is the key," too?!

00:17:48.380 --> 00:17:52.260
If you tried hard enough, I bet 
that would make a great pun!

00:17:52.570 --> 00:17:54.870
Key and key... The key is the key.

00:17:54.870 --> 00:17:57.640
The key's a key, too! The key's key!

00:17:55.600 --> 00:17:56.850
I'm changing back.

00:18:04.150 --> 00:18:05.020
Huh?

00:18:05.560 --> 00:18:07.870
Were you two done talking?

00:18:07.870 --> 00:18:08.890
Y-Yeah!

00:18:09.350 --> 00:18:13.570
That Yue, he just changed right 
back, without sayin' goodbye...

00:18:13.570 --> 00:18:15.040
Um, sorry!

00:18:15.570 --> 00:18:18.690
If only Yue were as genuine 
as you, Yukibunny...

00:18:18.690 --> 00:18:21.790
Of course, if he tried to be genuine, 
he wouldn't be Yue!

00:18:22.470 --> 00:18:24.060
Really?

00:18:25.130 --> 00:18:29.590
Someday, I'd love to meet the other me.

00:18:30.810 --> 00:18:32.320
Yukito-san...

00:18:35.100 --> 00:18:36.960
I guess the tea got cold, huh?

00:18:36.960 --> 00:18:37.920
I'll make some more.

00:18:38.490 --> 00:18:41.280
I also have some nerikiri and mizu manju.

00:18:41.280 --> 00:18:44.290
Yeah! Yay!

00:18:42.490 --> 00:18:44.230
I'll help you.

00:18:44.230 --> 00:18:45.250
Thanks.

00:18:44.290 --> 00:18:46.050
Anko!

00:18:46.360 --> 00:18:48.160
Yay!

00:18:48.160 --> 00:18:49.900
Anko! Anko! Anko!

00:18:51.260 --> 00:18:52.430
Anko—

00:18:52.430 --> 00:18:53.990
Hey, Sakura-chan...

00:18:53.990 --> 00:18:54.830
Yes?

00:18:55.680 --> 00:18:57.020
Have you talked to Toya?

00:18:57.020 --> 00:18:58.200
Onii-chan!

00:18:58.750 --> 00:19:01.650
This morning, he dumped 
all his broccoli on me,

00:19:01.650 --> 00:19:04.650
and he told me to become a monster!

00:19:04.650 --> 00:19:06.060
I see...

00:19:06.490 --> 00:19:08.870
You two really are close, huh?

00:19:08.870 --> 00:19:09.950
We are not!

00:19:12.080 --> 00:19:14.170
Do you have a cold, Mr. Bunny?

00:19:17.340 --> 00:19:19.980
<i>That's Sakura talking about me, isn't it?</i>

00:19:20.390 --> 00:19:23.750
<i>Tomorrow, she's getting a 
konjac combo for breakfast!</i>

00:19:28.640 --> 00:19:31.400
<b>Syaoran-kun</b>

00:19:29.440 --> 00:19:30.550
Phone call?

00:19:30.550 --> 00:19:31.400
Yeah.

00:19:31.810 --> 00:19:33.290
It's okay. You can answer it.

00:19:33.840 --> 00:19:35.950
I'll be waiting in the kitchen.

00:19:35.950 --> 00:19:37.550
Thank you.

00:19:39.100 --> 00:19:40.300
This is Sakura.

00:19:40.660 --> 00:19:42.160
<i>Do you have time to talk?</i>

00:19:42.160 --> 00:19:45.260
Sure. I'm at Yukito-san's house.

00:19:45.960 --> 00:19:47.270
<i>What did Yue think?</i>

00:19:50.020 --> 00:19:52.690
He still couldn't sense any magic.

00:19:53.170 --> 00:19:56.170
And it seemed like he didn't notice 
anything new, as well

00:19:56.720 --> 00:19:57.800
<i>I see.</i>

00:19:58.500 --> 00:20:01.500
Eriol-kun still hasn't replied, either.

00:20:02.500 --> 00:20:03.610
<i>I see.</i>

00:20:04.840 --> 00:20:07.300
There's a lot I don't understand,

00:20:07.300 --> 00:20:10.000
but I'm going to do whatever I can.

00:20:10.510 --> 00:20:12.400
I'll start with what's front of me!

00:20:12.910 --> 00:20:14.400
<i>You're pretty amazing, Sakura.</i>

00:20:14.400 --> 00:20:15.020
Huh?

00:20:15.020 --> 00:20:18.700
No, I'm not! You're way 
more amazing than I am!

00:20:18.700 --> 00:20:20.410
You're living by yourself, and...

00:20:20.410 --> 00:20:22.020
Oh, that reminds me... Listen...

00:20:26.320 --> 00:20:30.100
Would it be okay... if I 
made a lunch for you?

00:20:30.100 --> 00:20:31.020
<i>For me?</i>

00:20:31.370 --> 00:20:32.290
Yeah.

00:20:32.580 --> 00:20:35.640
I've been practicing, 
so I don't burn the eggs.

00:20:35.640 --> 00:20:39.100
My brother's still taste better, though...

00:20:39.100 --> 00:20:41.860
<i>Thanks. I'll look forward to it.</i>

00:20:42.840 --> 00:20:43.790
I'll do my best.

00:20:44.860 --> 00:20:47.620
<i>If anything unusual happens, call me.</i>

00:20:48.050 --> 00:20:49.370
<i>Even at night.</i>

00:20:50.320 --> 00:20:51.190
Okay.

00:20:52.510 --> 00:20:53.680
And, um...

00:20:53.680 --> 00:20:54.660
<i>What?</i>

00:20:57.190 --> 00:21:02.420
Can I call you, even if... 
nothing unusual is going on?

00:21:07.210 --> 00:21:08.170
<i>Any time.</i>

00:21:09.640 --> 00:21:12.190
Thanks, Syaoran-kun!

00:21:12.410 --> 00:21:15.210
<b>End Call</b>

00:21:15.210 --> 00:21:16.460
<b>Call Ended</b>

00:21:20.460 --> 00:21:24.550
<b>Syaoran Li</b>

00:21:27.220 --> 00:21:28.380
How did it go?

00:21:28.920 --> 00:21:32.800
<i>She said both Yue and Cerberus 
didn't notice anything.</i>

00:21:33.310 --> 00:21:36.800
<i>The only unusual thing is a new 
student joining her class.</i>

00:21:37.160 --> 00:21:38.390
A new student?

00:21:38.820 --> 00:21:39.600
<i>Yeah.</i>

00:21:41.850 --> 00:21:43.630
<i>A girl, right?</i>

00:21:43.630 --> 00:21:46.790
Yeah. I didn't sense any magic in her.

00:21:47.330 --> 00:21:49.110
<i>My readings show the same thing.</i>

00:21:49.770 --> 00:21:50.760
<i>Anything else?</i>

00:21:51.610 --> 00:21:52.680
Nothing.

00:21:55.230 --> 00:21:58.420
Only that she and Sakura-san get along well.

00:21:58.420 --> 00:22:00.370
They should become good friends.

00:22:01.180 --> 00:22:02.310
<i>I see.</i>

00:22:03.140 --> 00:22:04.780
Has anything else happened?

00:22:05.530 --> 00:22:08.590
<i>Another new card showed up.</i>

00:22:10.790 --> 00:22:13.700
<i>I'm sure it's hard on you, 
but this is not the time.</i>

00:22:14.180 --> 00:22:15.330
I know.

00:22:16.790 --> 00:22:20.780
I came here to be ready for 
that time, when it comes.

00:24:10.470 --> 00:24:12.170
Hidey-howdy-ho!

00:24:11.590 --> 00:24:12.970
<b>Leave It to Kero-chan!</b>

00:24:12.970 --> 00:24:19.850
<b>Bear      Cat</b>

00:24:12.970 --> 00:24:19.850
<b>K</b>

00:24:13.180 --> 00:24:15.950
It's the "Leave It to Kero-chan!" 
segment you've been waitin' for.

00:24:15.950 --> 00:24:17.260
Today, we'll meet

00:24:17.260 --> 00:24:20.200
the teachers at Tomoeda Middle School!

00:24:20.200 --> 00:24:23.440
The homeroom teacher with the cute, 
short hair is Morita-sensei.

00:24:23.440 --> 00:24:25.950
She seems real nice, and the 
subject she teaches is Japanese.

00:24:25.950 --> 00:24:29.080
Her assistant, Mori-sensei, is also 
the Cheerleading Club adviser.

00:24:29.080 --> 00:24:32.190
Then, there's the teacher for math, 
Sakura's worst subject, and science—

00:24:31.200 --> 00:24:32.200
<b>They're too lesser-known for this...</b>

00:24:32.200 --> 00:24:37.370
<b>Bear      Cat</b>

00:24:32.200 --> 00:24:37.370
<b>K</b>

00:24:32.740 --> 00:24:35.630
The kanji on the Clear Cards is 
gettin' harder to read, huh?

00:24:35.630 --> 00:24:38.370
It'll be good practice for Sakura, 
now that she's in middle school!

00:24:38.370 --> 00:24:39.690
Ta-ta!

00:24:40.000 --> 00:24:42.000
<b>Next Episode</b>

00:24:40.550 --> 00:24:44.630
I invited Akiho-chan to go see the 
cherry blossoms with all of us.

00:24:44.630 --> 00:24:47.750
I hope the rolled omelets I'm making 
for our lunch turn out okay...

00:24:48.310 --> 00:24:51.250
Next time, "Sakura Feels a Pull 
at the Flower Viewing."

00:24:49.250 --> 00:24:55.010
<b>Sakura Feels a Pull at the Flower Viewing</b>

00:24:51.560 --> 00:24:54.550
Say it with me: "Release!"

00:24:55.010 --> 00:25:00.010
<b>End</b>
